<text xml:lang="ta" type="edition">
  <body>
    <div rend="parallel"> 
      <p xml:id="Aink191-kilavi">
       niṉṉāl kāṇappaṭṭavaḷ evviṭattu ettaṉmaiyaḷ eṉṟu viṉāviya pāṅkaṟku talaimakaṉ kūṟiyatu.</p>    <p xml:lang="en">
       Spoken by the hero to [his] male friend, who asked, 'The girl who was seen by you, what kind of nature does she have [and] of which place [is she]?'.</p>
  </div> 
    <div rend="parallel">
      <lg xml:id="Aink191">
<l>kaṭaṟkōṭu ceṟinta vaḷaivār muṉkaik</l>
<l>kaḻippūt toṭarnta virumpal kūntaṟ</l>
<l>kāṉaṉ ñāḻaṟ kaviṉpeṟu taḻaiyaḷ</l>
<l>varaiyara makaḷiri ṉariyaḷeṉ</l>
<l>ṉiṟaiyaru neñcaṅ koṇṭoḷit tōḷē</l>
      </lg>
      <lg xml:lang="en">
        <l>The girl with the leaf skirt that has beauty, like the Ñāḻal tree in the seashore grove</l>
        <l>[With] forearms overflowing with dense bangles of sea-conch,</l>
        <l>[And] dark, many hairs to which flowers from the backwaters were linked,</l>
        <l>She who is rarer than the mountain-nymph ladies,</l>
        <l>Has hidden my resolute, rare heart, having taken [it away].</l>
              </lg>
    </div>
  </body>
</text>
